  "contracts": [
    "Keep each BF16 channel mean at its original pre-Engram layer and generation. Direct mean output into its strided packet slice avoids a second pack only when the backend supports those strides and the buffer stays live. One ordered TP8 gather after the third mean may replace three. It must have the same participants and collective ordering on all peers. For known padded prefix all three local rows are still sent per owner; 3*3*5120*2 = 92160 B/rank before and after.",
    "Reuse the packet as [N,15360] without a Cat only for the proven prefix or a compatible view. Nonpadded late selection needs ordered reconstruction, including duplicates and negative index behavior. SP-off has no gather credit. K0, skipped draft or a non-owning PP rank do not justify moving the main projection. Extra readers or outstanding graph buffers need the original lifetime and visibility.",
    "Six isolated BF16 fixtures gave identical selected input and unchanged-M projection. Precomputing a different M before taking the same indices produced mismatches in two of six. The dense main GEMM, its feature gather, transpose and RMS are preserved. Earlier execution of the same GEMM would be separate scheduling credit.",
    "The three mean computations remain. The indexed/Cat tasks in the old pack-only estimate are included once here. No credit for final target HcPost, WKV, SWA delivery, CPU waits or tile work. Never sum this packet with an alternative already removing the same checkpoint gather."
  ],
  "pricing": [
    "Eager uses the actual three disjoint TP collectives captured between each ReduceMean and next HcPre and the three exact IndexCheck/Index pairs where present plus ConcatD before the original DSpark main MatMul. Use min/max at latest participant entry using archived clock offset bounds. C8 includes both DPs and actual graph frequencies at every frozen request deadline.",
    "Graph compute uses separate archived same-shape native samples: 48 matched M24 windows for the three original collectives and the packing chain; frozen eager short q3 examples for M6 and M12; interpolate M18. Zero to largest observed elapsed per old gather allows the old rank wait to be entirely exposed on the optimistic side. These are cohort projections, not guaranteed graph bounds. Double-graph-free doubles even those gross graph credits at fixed eager costs.",
    "Free-named-tasks erases three original gathers and every confirmed packing task at zero cost, keeping mean and projection. Packet estimates charge a new 3q*5120 BF16 gather. Small transfers interpolate the existing tuned or default concurrent TP8 calibration. For large transfers use a startup-plus-payload model at the old effective rate and include a sensitivity with 25% longer payload time. Strided-store or scheduling penalties would reduce benefit.",
    "For ordinary traffic interpolate no-spec prompt concatenation and producer transfers through the original per-owner shapes, then apply the one-request M6 graph estimate for its observed verification count. These requests have no archived per-kernel profile for the proposed change; local costs and exposure can differ."
  ],
